/*  The tree the parser builds, and how it is printed.

    ★ ONE node type for every kind of node. A node is its KIND — the name of the C# record it
    stands for, `BinaryExpression`, `DefineStatement` — and its children in that record's field
    order. A leaf (a name, a number, a line) is an `atom` holding the text it prints as, and a
    list of things is a `list`. That is the whole of it, and it is exactly the shape the answer key
    prints: `ParserTreePrinter` walks the C# tree by reflection, one field at a time.

    ★ Printed into a chase rather than joined as text — a program's tree is a long line, and
    joining it a piece at a time would copy it once per piece.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Define object node with (the text kind, the text word, the series of node children).

    /// A node of one kind, with no children yet.
    Bind node to shaped, given (the text kind):
        Return a new node { the kind kind, the word "", the children a series of node }.
    Done.

    /// A leaf, printed exactly as `word`.
    Bind node to atom, given (the text word):
        Return a new node { the kind "atom", the word word, the children a series of node }.
    Done.

    Bind node to listed:
        Return a new node { the kind "list", the word "", the children a series of node }.
    Done.

    /// What the printer writes for a field holding nothing.
    Bind node to nothing:
        Return cast atom on ("_").
    Done.

    /// A text, in quotes, with the characters that would break a line or a quote escaped.
    Bind node to quoted, given (the text raw):
        Define shown as replace "\\" with "\\\\" in raw.
        The shown becomes replace "\"" with "\\\"" in shown.
        The shown becomes replace "\n" with "\\n" in shown.
        The shown becomes replace "\t" with "\\t" in shown.
        The shown becomes replace "\r" with "\\r" in shown.
        Return cast atom on ("\"" joined to shown joined to "\"").
    Done.

    Bind node to numeral, given (the number amount):
        Return cast atom on (amount converted to text).
    Done.

    Bind node to flag, given (the fact truth):
        Return cast atom on (truth converted to text).
    Done.

    Bind void to add unto node, given (the node child):
        Insert child into one's children.
    Done.

    /// `(Kind a b)`, `[a b]`, or a leaf's own text.
    Bind void to write-tree, given (the node tree, the chase out):
        If tree's kind is "atom":
            Insert tree's word into out.
            Return.
        Done.
        Define closer as ")".
        If tree's kind is "list":
            Insert "[" into out.
            The closer becomes "]".
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Insert "(" into out.
            Insert tree's kind into out.
        Done.
        Define opening as tree's kind is "list".
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            If opening is false, insert " " into out.
            The opening becomes false.
            Cast write-tree on (child, out).
        Done.
        Insert closer into out.
    Done.

    Bind text to shown-tree, given (the node tree):
        Define out as a chase.
        Cast write-tree on (tree, out).
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.
Done.
